  <running_head>INSTITUTIONUM</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>de explicatur, si aperiatur objectum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>instrumentum &amp; modus, quae eadem etiam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>circa reliquas virtutes fuerunt declarata.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">II. <i>Objectum idem est quod appeti-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>tus, nempe bonum &amp; malum: quia ut ap-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>petitus potiatur appetito motus localis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>et attributus est.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">§. Hoc clarissime docuit Arist. l. 3.</l>
    <l n="9">de anim. c.10. &amp; l. de animal. mot.c.4.</l>
    <l n="10">&amp; nihil difficultatis habet.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">III. <i>Instrumentum motus musculus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>est, spiritibus sufficienter impragnatus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">§. Aristot. l. de mot. animal.c.5.ner-</l>
    <l n="14">vos &amp; ossa videtur indigitare, &amp; cap.8.</l>
    <l n="15">spiritus vitales, quo loco etiam docet</l>
    <l n="16">cor esse primum motus principium</l>
    <l n="17">corporale. Nam in corde radicari ani-</l>
    <l n="18">mam supra tetigimus, &amp; hoc loco do-</l>
    <l n="19">cere videtur Philosophus ulterius in</l>
    <l n="20">corde solitarie existere, atque in</l>
    <l n="21">reliquo corpore per spiritus operari. In hoc</l>
    <l n="22">Philosophi dogmate illud supponen-</l>
    <l n="23">dum est, verum esse, animam sensitivam</l>
    <l n="24">esse primam motionis animalis cau-</l>
    <l n="25">sam, sicuti bene docuit l.3.de anim.c.10.</l>
    <l n="26">atque l.de mot.anim.c.3. Deinde neque</l>
    <l n="27">male ab ipso doceri cordis &amp; spiritus</l>
    <l n="28">vitalis operationem ad motum requiri,</l>
    <l n="29">licet non concedamus soli cordi ani-</l>
    <l n="30">mam inexistere: Id quoque largimur verum</l>
  </main_text>
